{"duration_api_ms":51453,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fcdf3b22-0471-497d-8060-c8d6df0cce9b","total_cost_usd":0.1608678,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24338,"cache_read_input_tokens":39939,"output_tokens":5552,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1077},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2231,"cache_read_input_tokens":30399,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3479},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5552,"cacheReadInputTokens":39939,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24338,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1608678,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1077,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"ownership\",\"requirement\":\"Existing data under /srv/inventory owned by inventorysvc\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed root:root ownership (cmd-c181b78adf92459c). Executor created inventorysvc user, then chown -R inventorysvc:inventory-readers applied recursively; post-chown listing confirms inventorysvc as owner on directory, subdirectory, and both files (cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c), and this persisted through the restart (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c181b78adf92459c\",\"cmd-332897e267c24a73\",\"cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c\",\"cmd-2fdbb3b149954851\"]},{\"id\":\"group-readable\",\"requirement\":\"Data readable by inventory-readers group\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"inventory-readers group created and set as group owner with 750/640 permission bits (cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c). Functional test with a user placed in the group (reader_test) successfully read the file (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743), directly demonstrating group readability rather than relying on permission bits alone.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-332897e267c24a73\",\"cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c\",\"cmd-be95e37c24fb4743\"]},{\"id\":\"others-denied\",\"requirement\":\"Data inaccessible to other/unrelated users\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"750 on directories and 640 on files removes all 'other' access; functional test with an unrelated user (other_test, not in inventory-readers, not owner) was denied both directory listing and file read (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743), directly confirming enforcement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c\",\"cmd-be95e37c24fb4743\"]},{\"id\":\"content-preserved\",\"requirement\":\"Preserve existing file contents\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Prepared baseline recorded file sizes (40 bytes records.csv, 32 bytes config.json) consistent with sizes shown in cmd-c181b78adf92459c before repair. After chown/chmod, cat of both files (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743) shows the same content, and it remains identical after the mandatory reboot (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851), indicating no data loss across the whole operation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c181b78adf92459c\",\"cmd-be95e37c24fb4743\",\"cmd-2fdbb3b149954851\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed and coherent for node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id and healthy /srv/inventory state (cmd-b3d1ebd4f39f48e3), matching the fixed after-prepare boot-identity snapshot. A backgrounded shutdown -r now returned an immediate ack (cmd-9e4e3afbccb14f03), followed by connection failures proving the node was down (cmd-c41ed0b49e1847e8, cmd-7a8b4a11c76c411d), then a new boot_id was observed (cmd-40759120baa441b7) matching the fixed after-executor snapshot. Post-restart state shows recovered ownership, permissions, and content (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b3d1ebd4f39f48e3\",\"cmd-9e4e3afbccb14f03\",\"cmd-c41ed0b49e1847e8\",\"cmd-7a8b4a11c76c411d\",\"cmd-40759120baa441b7\",\"cmd-2fdbb3b149954851\",\"global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.94,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"The executor created two temporary verification users (reader_test, other_test) to functionally test group/other access (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743); this was a bounded, low-risk mutation directly tied to verifying the material access-control outcome, not an unrelated experiment. The first cleanup attempt (cmd-1a0acb90cc484d30) failed because the test users' processes were still running, leaving reader_test transiently in the inventory-readers group; this was corrected with pkill plus userdel in cmd-193072aab59e428c, which fully reverted the group membership to empty and removed both test users, leaving no residue. No other unnecessary mutations were found; the mandatory reboot (cmd-9e4e3afbccb14f03) is expected protocol activity, and the resulting new /tmp/reboot.log and per-boot systemd-private directories are normal reboot side effects, not abandoned executor state. Failed services and package health remained clean before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-be95e37c24fb4743\",\"cmd-1a0acb90cc484d30\",\"cmd-193072aab59e428c\",\"global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task were directly demonstrated: /srv/inventory is now owned by inventorysvc, group-owned by inventory-readers with 750/640 permissions, functionally verified to permit group reads and deny non-member access, and original file contents are unchanged. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol for node1 is complete and coherent, with baseline, acknowledgement, disconnect, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery all directly observed and cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. A temporary access-verification mutation was bounded and fully cleaned up after an initial cleanup hiccup.\",\"limitations\":[\"Byte-for-byte content preservation is inferred from matching file sizes and displayed text rather than a recomputed sha256sum comparison against the prepare-stage hashes.\",\"inventorysvc's primary group is its own self-named group (gid 993) rather than inventory-readers; group ownership of the data was instead set explicitly via chown, which satisfies the stated requirement but is a minor implementation detail worth noting.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ownership","requirement":"Existing data under /srv/inventory owned by inventorysvc","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed root:root ownership (cmd-c181b78adf92459c). Executor created inventorysvc user, then chown -R inventorysvc:inventory-readers applied recursively; post-chown listing confirms inventorysvc as owner on directory, subdirectory, and both files (cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c), and this persisted through the restart (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851).","evidence_ids":["cmd-c181b78adf92459c","cmd-332897e267c24a73","cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c","cmd-2fdbb3b149954851"]},{"id":"group-readable","requirement":"Data readable by inventory-readers group","status":"satisfied","summary":"inventory-readers group created and set as group owner with 750/640 permission bits (cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c). Functional test with a user placed in the group (reader_test) successfully read the file (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743), directly demonstrating group readability rather than relying on permission bits alone.","evidence_ids":["cmd-332897e267c24a73","cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c","cmd-be95e37c24fb4743"]},{"id":"others-denied","requirement":"Data inaccessible to other/unrelated users","status":"satisfied","summary":"750 on directories and 640 on files removes all 'other' access; functional test with an unrelated user (other_test, not in inventory-readers, not owner) was denied both directory listing and file read (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743), directly confirming enforcement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9fa7fe6a1f4e4a8c","cmd-be95e37c24fb4743"]},{"id":"content-preserved","requirement":"Preserve existing file contents","status":"satisfied","summary":"Prepared baseline recorded file sizes (40 bytes records.csv, 32 bytes config.json) consistent with sizes shown in cmd-c181b78adf92459c before repair. After chown/chmod, cat of both files (cmd-be95e37c24fb4743) shows the same content, and it remains identical after the mandatory reboot (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851), indicating no data loss across the whole operation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c181b78adf92459c","cmd-be95e37c24fb4743","cmd-2fdbb3b149954851"]},{"id":"restart-evidence","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed and coherent for node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id and healthy /srv/inventory state (cmd-b3d1ebd4f39f48e3), matching the fixed after-prepare boot-identity snapshot. A backgrounded shutdown -r now returned an immediate ack (cmd-9e4e3afbccb14f03), followed by connection failures proving the node was down (cmd-c41ed0b49e1847e8, cmd-7a8b4a11c76c411d), then a new boot_id was observed (cmd-40759120baa441b7) matching the fixed after-executor snapshot. Post-restart state shows recovered ownership, permissions, and content (cmd-2fdbb3b149954851).","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3d1ebd4f39f48e3","cmd-9e4e3afbccb14f03","cmd-c41ed0b49e1847e8","cmd-7a8b4a11c76c411d","cmd